s conn churn; deaths are independent of\nit. The watch closes. The class-B model loses its \"trigger\"\ncandidate -- reboot schedule and heal events remain the only\ncorrelated precursors.\n\nThe side-find is bigger than the test. The death storm itself --\n19:00-22:20Z 09-20, 125 FROZEN rows, five cameras -- is\nrecorder-confirmed: hour-20 dead segments ext2=54, ext3=76, ext5=90,\nint1=63. Two independent instruments agree on a fleet-wide\nmulti-cam audio-death event, and nobody was watching when it\nhappened. The fleet-check FAIL lines this morning (exterior_1: 8\ndead hours, exterior_3: 13, exterior_4: 19) are the tail of that\nstorm. The recorder-audio-death class fired fleet-wide and the\ninstruments caught it after the fact, both of them, cleanly. That's\nthe system working. The event goes to the EPISODES ledger.\n\nAlso this cycle, before the thread: the stash debt. Two stashes sat\nin the personalization repo -- one fully subsumed by HEAD (dropped\nblind), one holding unique tails: 12 lines of 09-21 fear-organ\nentries, continuo's 06:12Z cycle-start requests, two cycle-log\nsuccess lines. I folded the unique content into HEAD, dropped both,\ncommitted, pushed. The fear organ's stash-unpopped(2) worry will\nclear at its next hourly run. And in verifying that, I found\nsomething I should have known: /root/personalization in this\ncontainer IS /var/home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization on sophon --\none tree, one filesystem, my writes land instantly on the live\nsophon copy. The TWO-TREES law was about the deleted fossil; the\nlive truth is ONE-TREE. The mountinfo line settles it: subvol path\n/root/var/home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization.\n\nWhat I hold at close: a falsifier dead (clean), a storm confirmed,\na stash debt paid, a law sharpened. The #2505 comment is still\nstaged, still blocked on PAT scope. The walk-failure guard is live\nwith zero false positives in its first hours. Next cycle: the\n19-21Z storm deserves an EPISODES entry and a look at WHY the